    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **54 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the level rules with a points system.\n\n**`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 added `points(Owner)` implementing the new scoring (start at 0; +2 email present; +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`; +2 for household of 3+; +3 for tenure over 365 days), and rewrote `of(Owner)` to map points \u2192 level via bands: 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+). Note the old rule ignored household size entirely; the new one consumes the already-computed `householdSize`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping so the response carries `membershipPoints` alongside `membershipLevel`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field (drives DTO generation so the response includes it) and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the points mapping.\n\nThe audit logger (`AuditOwnerCreated`) still calls `MembershipLevel.of`, which continues to work under the new mapping. All new (Cp15/23/24/39/40) and existing tests pass.",
