    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the complete ordered list of everything `POST /api/owners` applies, from the endpoint YAML (`owners.POST.yml`) and its function classes.\n\n## Pre-check (gate)\n\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\nEvery step below runs inside a single `transaction` governance that spans the pipeline and commits once at the end.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields`\nRuns first, on the request body (`OwnerFieldsDto`). In this exact internal order:\n\n1. **Normalize address** (side-effect, mutates request): trim, collapse whitespace runs to one space, upper-case, expand street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); null/blank \u2192 `\"\"`.\n2. **Required-field validation** (after address normalization): reject if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400), listing every missing field. (Note: because address is normalized first, an address blank-after-normalization is caught here.)\n3. **Normalize telephone** (validation + side-effect): convert to E.164 \u2014 strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep `+` and country code if present, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; require 8\u201315 digits; for known codes enforce national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (400). Stores the E.164 form.\n4. **Validate/normalize email** (only when present/non-blank): trim, syntax-check, reject disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerEmailException` (400). Stores lower-cased.\n5. **Validate/normalize postcode** (only when present/non-blank): must be 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region, must fall in its range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); otherwise any 4 digits accepted. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` (400). Stores the trimmed value.\n6. **Validate registration date** (only when present): must not be after the server's current date (checked as-is, before business-day adjustment) \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n7. **Publish** the validated/normalized request as a variable for later steps.\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n8. Map the DTO to an `Owner` entity (via `OwnerMapper`).\n9. **Set registration date** to the *effective business day*: supplied date or today, with a Saturday/Sunday rolled forward to the next Monday.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `AssignHousehold`\n10. Stamp `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)` (null postcode \u2192 empty segment). Deterministic; no lookup.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`\n11. **Household-duplicate check**: unless the request set `sharesHousehold: true`, scan all existing owners; if any share this `householdId`, reject \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409). `sharesHousehold` bypasses this check only.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\n12. **Identity-duplicate check** (never bypassed): compute `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId` and reject if it exactly matches any existing owner's \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n13. **City capacity check**: reject if the request's city (case-insensitive) already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409). Count excludes the new owner.\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\n14. **Daily limit check**: reject if \u2265 100 existing owners already have this owner's effective (business-day-adjusted) registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429). Count excludes the new owner.\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `AssignHouseholdSize`\n15. Set `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus 1 for this owner (1 if `householdId` is null).\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode`\n16. Set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode with city fallback; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized telephone + last name).\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount`\n17. Set `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing `firstName`+`lastName` (case-insensitive), excluding the new owner.\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n18. Set `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Then, unless `sharesHousehold` is true (and only if lastName/postcode/telephone all present), scan existing owners for one sharing lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but a **different** telephone; if found, set `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = smallest matching owner id.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n19. **Persist** the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n20. **Audit log** (side-effect): emit an `AUDIT` logger line with owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, and numeric membershipLevel.\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n21. Map the saved owner to `OwnerDto`, compute and set `bulkSignupWarning` (true if > 80 owners already share this effective registration day), and respond **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n### Notes\n- **Validations** (short-circuit with an error): steps 2\u20136 (400s), and steps 11\u201314 duplicate/capacity/limit checks (409s/429).\n- **Mutating side-effects on the entity/request**: address/telephone/email/postcode normalization, registration-date business-day adjustment, and the assigned `householdId`, `householdSize`, `customerCode`, `namesakeCount`, `possibleDuplicate*` fields.\n- **External side-effects**: the DB save and the audit log line; the response itself (201 + Location + `bulkSignupWarning`)."
